DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("sqrt((((x^3))^(1/4)))");
$fun_1 = Formula("(e^(x))+5");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("({-10, -8, -3, 0, 5, 9} - {-10, 2, 7, 9})");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("[0, 10] - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-10, -8, -3, 0, 5, 9}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-10, 2, 7, 9})");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("({-10, 2, 7, 9} U {-10, 2, 7, 9}) U [0, 10] U [0, 10] U {-10, 2, 7, 9}");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("({-5, 7} U ({-9, -7, 5, 8, 9} U {-5, 7}) U {-5, 7}) U {-9, -7, 5, 8, 9} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-9, -7, 5, 8, 9}) U (({-9, -7, 5, 8, 9}))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-9, -7, 5, 8, 9} U (({-5, 7}))");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("{-9, -7, 5, 8, 9} U ({-9, -7, 5, 8, 9} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-5, 7})) U {-5, 7}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`15+10-9+19`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>35,width=>10}
---

[`9+4+14+13/12`] is equal to [_____]{Real(28.0833333333)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-9, -7, 5, 8, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{-5, 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`(B \cup (A \cup B) \cup B) \cup A \cap A \cup ((A)) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup ((B)) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`A \cup (A \cap B) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-10, -8, -3, 0, 5, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{-10, 2, 7, 9\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 0 \leq x \leq 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`A - B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`C \cap A \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`(B \cup B) \cup C \cup C \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 6, 0, -1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -2, 6, 9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -2, 7, 6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, 6, 9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, 6, 9>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, 7, 6>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<6, 0, -1>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-2, 7, 6>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-2, 6, 9>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -7, 9, -7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -3, 8, 8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-7, 9, -7>") . Compute("<-3, 8, 8>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, 8, 8>") . Compute("<-7, 9, -7>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, 9, -7>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-7, 9, -7>") x Compute("<-3, 8, 8>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-7, 9, -7>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>5)}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>9)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(8) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>8)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>6)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
